This project has two halves, and they are licensed differently on purpose.

  THE CODE            open to read, closed to use.      Part A below.
  THE DICTIONARY      open to everyone, for anything.   Part B below.

The software is published so it can be read and learned from, not so it can be
copied, deployed or sold. The words are the opposite: they belong to the people
who speak the language, and anyone may take them and do as they wish.

