===============================================================================
PART B. THE DICTIONARY CONTENT
===============================================================================

Applies to the words themselves: every Sasak headword, translation, Indonesian
gloss, example sentence, usage note, dialect attribution and recording
submitted to SAWAH by contributors.

B1. LICENCE

    Dictionary Content is released under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
    International licence (CC BY 4.0).

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

    You may copy it, publish it, translate it, build on it, print it, feed it to
    a language model, put it in a textbook, or sell something made from it. You
    do not need permission and you do not need to ask.

    The single condition is credit: say it came from SAWAH, and link back where
    it is reasonable to do so.

B2. WHY IT IS OPEN

    A language does not belong to whoever built the website that recorded it. It
    belongs to the people who speak it. Locking Sasak words behind the same
    terms as the software would make this project a worse version of the problem
    it exists to fix.

    Nothing in Part A restricts Part B. Where the two appear to conflict, Part B
    wins for content and Part A wins for code.

B3. CONTRIBUTORS

    By submitting Dictionary Content you agree it is released under CC BY 4.0 as
    described above, and you confirm you have the right to submit it.

    Contributions are credited to an anonymous handle rather than a name, and
    attribution under B1 is to SAWAH as a whole rather than to individual
    contributors.
